# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# A row is as tall as the letters in it, and the letters are a preference.
#
# The height was worked out once, when the shell started, and handed to
# everything that draws a list -- so changing the face redrew the words at
# their new size into rows still sized for the old one.  At 16 px they did
# not fit; the fix is that the height is taken again every frame.
#
# Asked here the only way a script can see it: how many rows the window
# SHOWS.  A taller row means fewer of them in the same window, which is
# arithmetic no redraw can fake.
wait 15
expect-visible-rows 10
note put the interface up to 16 px from the window that chooses it
click 980 20
wait 4
menu-pick Settings
wait 4
menu-pick Fonts
wait 12
expect-title Fonts
expect-font Sans 12
click 652 300
wait 12
expect-font Sans 14
click 652 310
wait 12
expect-font Sans 16
note and back to the folder, whose rows are now taller than they were
key w ctrl
wait 8
expect-visible-rows 8
